> Let $f(n)$ be maximal such that for any $A\subseteq\mathbb{N}$ with $|A|=n$, the product $\prod_{a\neq b\in A}(a+b)$ has at least $f(n)$ distinct prime factors. Is it true that $f(n)/\log n \to \infty$?

This is a **genuine open research problem** in number theory, posed by Erdős (referenced at erdosproblems.com/126). The state of the art is:

